 ### MS-NeRF
-MS-NeRF addresses rendering distortion and blurring caused by reflection or refraction (e.g., mirrors) where standard NeRF fails multi-view consistency. It represents the scene by a set of characteristic fields in parallel subspaces [S3]. It modifies NeRF output and volumetric rendering module to output density and features instead of density and color, generating multiple sets of density and features. Volumetric rendering generates multiple feature maps from the multiple sets of density and features. A Decoder MLP is applied in each subspace to decode RGB images. A Gate MLP obtains pixel-level weights for the feature maps. Features from each subspace are integrated by summation to obtain the final result [S3]. On synthetic, real, and RFFR data sets, the PSNR index is 2-4 points higher [S3].
